  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1111 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nHigh pressure will continue to build through the weekend into\nearly next week according to ensemble data, with high \nconfidence in well above normal conditions (highs in the 70s to \naround 80). No precip is expected in this time frame. \n\nToward the middle of next week around 5-10% of ensembles are \nshowing some light rain as a trough passes through the area,\nwhich is a decrease of around 5-10% from this time yesterday.\nWhile this time period has the greatest rain chances in the next\n7 days, it is still far more likely to be dry than to wet. There\nremains quite a bit of uncertainty with temperatures due to \nmodel spread. For example, NBM 25-75th percentile MaxT spread \nincreases to around 15 degrees on Tuesday and Wednesday next \nweek.",
